cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  DBS Annotator: bedside recording of deep brain stimulation programming
  sessions in an analysis-ready format
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lucia
    family-names: Poma
    email: lucia.poma@wysscenter.ch
    affiliation: Wyss Center for Bio and Neuroengineering, Geneva, Switzerland
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TODO: add before submission
repository-code: https://github.com/Brain-Modulation-Lab/DBSAnnotator
url: https://dbsannotator.readthedocs.io/
abstract: >-
  DBS Annotator records deep brain stimulation programming sessions at the
  bedside and writes them to BIDS-named tab-separated files, capturing the
  relationship between the stimulation delivered at each configuration and the
  clinical response observed. It runs fully offline on tablets and desktops, and
  produces PDF and Word reports for the patient record.
keywords:
  - deep brain stimulation
  - DBS programming
  - neuromodulation
  - clinical data capture
  - BIDS
  - Flutter
license: MIT
